<title>INDIA: India soybean prices fall further as supplies rise.</title>
<headline>India soybean prices fall further as supplies rise.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices fell further by 400-500 rupees per tonne on Tuesday on increased arrivals, traders said.</p>
<p>On Monday, traders had reported a fall of 300-400 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were also down on heavy selling by processing plants and refining units. Soyoil solvent fell 300 rupees and soyoil refined by 200 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were subdued. Soymeal yellow was quoted at $270-271 per tonne in ready delivery and at $265-266 per tonne for export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was offered at $120-121 per tonne for export. Rapeseed extraction was quoted at 4,125 rupees FOR Bedibunder and at $400 FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
